Package: SESSFclosures
Type: Package
Title: Spatial Closures of the Southern and Eastern Scalefish and Shark Fishery, 2005 to Now
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-10-18
Authors@R: c(
    person("Paul", "Burch", email = "paul.burch77@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = "CSIRO Environment"),
    person("Claude", role = "ctb",
           comment = paste("AI assistant (Anthropic, model Claude Opus 5.5).",
                           "Wrote the parsing, assembly and package code, compiled the",
                           "closure data and drafted the documentation, directed by",
                           "the maintainer.")))
Description: The boundaries of every spatial closure of the Southern and Eastern
    Scalefish and Shark Fishery (SESSF) written in the closures directions on the
    Federal Register of Legislation, from SESSF Direction No. 01 (May 2005) to the
    current compilation of the 2021 Closures Direction, with the dates each boundary
    was in force, the gear it closes, and the instrument, schedule and page where it
    is written. Functions return the closures in force on a date, test whether
    fishing positions fell inside a closure that applied to them, and give the
    source of each boundary. AFMA's own polygons of the 2016 and 2021 directions are
    included for comparison. Compiled with the assistance of Claude (Anthropic).
    Versions below 1.0.0 have not had their closure boundaries checked by a person.
